{"packet_id":"D073-01","doc_id":"D073","jurisdiction":"San Diego, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Just cause required to terminate a tenancy","requirement":"A landlord may not terminate a residential tenancy without just cause; the only allowed causes are the at-fault and no-fault just causes listed in the Division.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Residential rental property in San Diego; tenancy lasting more than 30 days. Fixed-term leases of three months or less are excluded. Properties and circumstances listed in section 98.0703 are exempt.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":"certificate_of_occupancy","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Exempt: certificate of occupancy within previous 15 years; owner-occupied single-family, duplex and shared housing"},"exemptions":"See section 98.0703: transient/tourist hotels; short-term rentals; deed-restricted affordable housing; most subsidized housing (not Section 8); Mobilehome Residency Law mobilehomes; institutional and non-profit transitional housing; dorms; owner-occupied shared housing, single-family and duplex; housing with a certificate of occupancy within the previous 15 years.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2023-06-24","citation":"San Diego Mun. Code § 98.0704","quoted_span":"A landlord shall not terminate a tenancy without just cause. For purposes of this Division, just cause includes at-fault just cause and no-fault just cause.","interaction":"Rights are in addition to state and federal law; the just cause requirement is consistent with California Civil Code § 1946.2.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D073-01","doc_id":"D073","jurisdiction":"San Diego, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Exemptions from the Residential Tenant Protections Division","requirement":"The Division's tenant protections do not apply to the listed residential rental properties or circumstances, including transient and tourist hotels, short-term rentals, deed-restricted affordable housing, and recently built housing.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lists which residential rental properties and circumstances fall outside the Division's protections, including recently constructed housing and owner-occupied small properties.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":"certificate_of_occupancy","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Exempt: certificate of occupancy within previous 15 years; owner-occupied single-family, duplex and shared housing"},"exemptions":"Transient/tourist hotels; short-term rentals; deed-restricted affordable housing; subsidized affordable housing (not Section 8); Mobilehome Residency Law mobilehomes; hospitals, religious, extended-care, adult residential and non-profit transitional housing; school dorms; owner-occupied shared housing, single-family homes and duplexes; housing with a certificate of occupancy within the previous 15 years.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2023-06-24","citation":"San Diego Mun. Code § 98.0703","quoted_span":"This Division shall not apply to the following types of residential rental properties or residential circumstances:","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D073-01","doc_id":"D073","jurisdiction":"San Diego, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Notice to tenants of residential tenant protections","requirement":"A landlord must give tenants a written notice in at least 12-point font, plus the Tenant Protection Guide, stating that state law limits rent increases and that local law requires a statement of cause in any termination notice.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Residential rental property subject to the Division; for tenancies existing before June 24, 2023, the notice was due within 90 days of that date.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2023-06-24","citation":"San Diego Mun. Code § 98.0705","quoted_span":"A landlord of residential rental property subject to this Division shall provide written notice in no less than 12-point font to the tenant, and in a manner that complies with California Civil Code section 1632, as may be amended, that states as follows:","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
